      "title": "Control from the dashboard",
      "description": "Let the swarmery dashboard stop this session's running turn and send it prompts. One background loop long-polls the daemon (loopback only, bearer token) for commands queued for this session alone; nothing runs inside a hook and no gating hook is registered. Off: no request goes to the command endpoints.",
      "default": false
    },
    "approvals": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "title": "Approvals in Swarmery",
      "description": "Routes each permission ask to the Swarmery approvals queue first, ahead of the dialog or auto mode's classifier; the shim/dialog takes over if the daemon is down or does not decide in time. Only the engine's own ask goes there (its allow and deny stand), a production deploy is still confirmed in the terminal, and an AskUserQuestion can be answered from the dashboard. In auto mode this puts the ask to the dashboard before the classifier would have settled it. Off: no tool.check or AskUserQuestion hook is registered and no request goes to the permission endpoint.",
      "default": false
    },
    "planBand": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "title": "Plan band",
      "description": "Show this session's swarmery plan phase in a band above the prompt (Phase n, its open criteria, [1] next phase, [2] open in Swarmery, [3] tick), add /phase [task-id] for the full checklist, draw a dashboard interview question (its JSON) as a card with the recommended option highlighted, and flag a turn that drifts off the phase with one line beneath its answer. Costs one small $.model.classify call per main-loop turn that edits files while a phase runs, plus a plan request (loopback, bearer token) at session start, after each turn and every 60 s. Off: no band, no command, no classification and no plan request.",
