      "default": false
    },
    "claimConflicts": {
      "type": "string",
      "title": "Hold conflicting writes",
      "description": "With swarm on: what happens when this session is about to Edit, Write, MultiEdit or NotebookEdit a file another live session holds a claim on. off: nothing is held, the line beneath the answer still says so. ask: the native permission dialog asks, naming the other session, in default/acceptEdits/plan; in auto/dontAsk/bypassPermissions, where no person would see the ask, the write is refused. deny: the write is refused in every mode. Bash commands are never checked (their target path cannot be read). With approvals on too, the ask goes to the Swarmery approvals queue first, as any ask does.",
